From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:27:42 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Windows 10 Mobile: pages and calls are told H.264 and VP8, no
 VP9 or AV1

A site that is told VP9 or AV1 plays sends that, and both are decoded on
the CPU on these phones; H.264 is the codec they are built to play. The
embedder's ContentRendererClient::IsDecoderSupportedVideoType answers for
canPlayType, MediaSource, MediaCapabilities, the HLS player and WebCodecs'
isConfigSupported; what it does not reach is closed here:

- WebRTC's codec factories (blink's video_codec_factory.cc) list H.264
  first, then VP8, and nothing else: SDP, getCapabilities and
  MediaCapabilities' "webrtc" answers all come from them.
- WebCodecs' VideoDecoder.configure() refuses what isConfigSupported()
  refuses.
- A file whose only picture is VP9 or AV1 fails to load instead of playing
  its sound over a blank frame, so that a <source> list goes on to its MP4.

"--vw-codecs=all" lifts it; media/base/video_codecs_w10m.h is the one
place the switch is read.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 media/base/video_codecs_w10m.h                | 30 +++++++
 media/filters/ffmpeg_demuxer.cc               | 35 ++++++++
 .../modules/webcodecs/video_decoder.cc        | 10 +++
 .../peerconnection/video_codec_factory.cc     | 89 +++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 164 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 media/base/video_codecs_w10m.h

diff --git a/media/base/video_codecs_w10m.h b/media/base/video_codecs_w10m.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a4f29e056c52e5e8d8d396a691d6871b1b5c6118
--- /dev/null
+++ b/media/base/video_codecs_w10m.h
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+// Copyright 2026 The Venetium-W10M Authors
+// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be
+// found in the LICENSE file.
+
+#ifndef MEDIA_BASE_VIDEO_CODECS_W10M_H_
+#define MEDIA_BASE_VIDEO_CODECS_W10M_H_
+
+#include "base/command_line.h"
+
+namespace media {
+
+// Windows 10 Mobile (Venetium): video is decoded in software there, so pages
+// and peers are offered H.264 and VP8 and nothing heavier. "--vw-codecs=all"
+// among the shell's switches lifts that, for comparing on a device, and this
+// is the one place the switch is read. Two places decide by it: the
+// embedder's ContentRendererClient::IsDecoderSupportedVideoType, which media
+// and Blink ask through media::IsDecoderSupportedVideoType, and WebRTC's
+// codec factories (blink's video_codec_factory.cc), which cannot ask the
+// embedder: that question may wait for the main thread, and the main thread
+// waits for the signaling thread while the factories are made.
+inline bool W10mEveryVideoCodec() {
+  static const bool every_codec =
+      base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess()->GetSwitchValueASCII(
+          "vw-codecs") == "all";
+  return every_codec;
+}
+
+}  // namespace media
+
+#endif  // MEDIA_BASE_VIDEO_CODECS_W10M_H_
diff --git a/media/filters/ffmpeg_demuxer.cc b/media/filters/ffmpeg_demuxer.cc
index 45d82a351a1bcdc7ef832d220d112cbd04516ca1..333694d028004d72415a5edbbae88dc6f3c7dc78 100644
